        "block_text_q9GKWQ": {
          "type": "block_text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is Elemental Water?",
            "text": "<p>Elemental Water is a unique hydration solution designed with a specific blend of molecular hydrogen, gold, and platinum. These noble metals are included in very small, safe amounts and have been carefully selected for their inert properties, meaning they do not actively react within the human body in harmful ways. Gold and platinum are often referred to as “noble metals” due to their resistance to oxidation and corrosion, which aligns with their role in protecting cells at the molecular level. Our patent-pending formula aims to maximize the health benefits of hydrogen by creating an environment where hydrogen’s antioxidant effects can be amplified.</p><p>The use of gold and platinum is based on preliminary studies that suggest these metals can enhance cellular processes and antioxidant action. However, it’s important to note that ongoing research is needed to confirm the synergistic effects of these elements with hydrogen water.</p>",
            "bordered": false
          }
        },
        "block_text_QNa9Pg": {
          "type": "block_text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is Hydrogen Water?",
            "text": "<p>Hydrogen water is regular water infused with molecular hydrogen (H₂), a powerful antioxidant that can provide several health benefits at the cellular level. Numerous independent studies have shown that hydrogen has strong antioxidative properties, enabling it to combat free radicals and oxidative stress effectively, thereby promoting cellular health and preventing premature aging.</p>",
            "bordered": true
          }
        },
        "block_text_9b4Fxw": {
          "type": "block_text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Research has indicated a number of potential benefits of hydrogen water, such as:",
            "text": "<h3>Reduction of Oxidative Stress and Inflammation</h3><p>Hydrogen acts as an antioxidant that specifically targets cytotoxic oxygen radicals, helping to reduce oxidative stress and inflammation. This has been demonstrated in a variety of studies, such as a publication in Nature Medicine, which found that inhalation of hydrogen gas could reduce oxidative stress in patients with Parkinson’s disease and other conditions. Additionally, research published in Antioxidants has noted that drinking hydrogen-rich water increases antioxidant enzyme activities and decreases inflammation biomarkers, thereby suggesting potential applications in managing inflammatory diseases <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8519836/#:~:text=Oxidative%20stress%20is%20involved%20in,in%20animal%20models%20of%20PD\" target=\"_blank\">[1</a>, <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9222692/\" target=\"_blank\">2]</a>.</p><h3>Hydration and Energy Enhancement</h3><p>Hydrogen water has also been found to increase energy levels, reduce fatigue, and enhance endurance. Studies like those published in Medical Gas Research have shown that hydrogen water can contribute to improvements in athletic performance and quicker recovery times by enhancing mitochondrial function—the cell’s energy-producing components <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8139351/#:~:text=HRW%20supplementation%20has%20been%20shown,men%20and%20women%20%5B18%5D\" target=\"_blank\">[3]</a>.</p><h3>Potential Health Applications</h3><p>Research suggests that hydrogen water might offer various other health benefits, such as aiding mental health, potentially treating conditions like metabolic syndrome, reducing cholesterol levels, and even having applications in conditions like cancer treatment, by reducing the side effects of radiation therapy. One study published in Diabetes, Metabolic Syndrome and Obesity demonstrated that hydrogen-rich water consumption improved cholesterol and glucose metabolism in patients with type 2 diabetes <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22146004/\" target=\"_blank\">[4</a>,<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19083400/\" target=\"_blank\">5]</a>.</p><p>These studies underline the efficacy of hydrogen water, but it’s important to note that many of these benefits are still under investigation and that more extensive human clinical trials are required to draw definitive conclusions.</p>",
            "bordered": false
          }
        },
        "block_img_XP664m": {
          "type": "block_img",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What Makes Elemental Water Different?",
            "text": "<p>While hydrogen water is already a significant advancement over regular water, Elemental Water takes it further by incorporating nano-infused hydrogen with gold and platinum. These elements do not only provide a unique chemical environment but also may enhance the action of hydrogen within the body. Although the majority of the independent testing has been conducted on hydrogen water alone, the added inert noble metals are considered safe, and ongoing research is exploring their potential in cellular health support.</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/water-particel-1.png"
          }
        },
        "block_text_jyT7mr": {
          "type": "block_text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Common Misconceptions and Competitor Comparisons",
            "text": "<p>Some consumers have concerns about the inclusion of metals like gold and platinum. It’s important to emphasize that these metals are used in trace, inert forms, making them biologically safe. The amounts present are far below any threshold that could lead to heavy metal accumulation or toxicity, as supported by existing safety standards.</p><p>In comparison to other hydrogen water products that often include flavorings, electrolytes, and other additives, Elemental Water focuses purely on delivering potent hydrogen without additives that could negatively interact with hydrogen. Additives like minerals and flavorings can react with hydrogen and reduce its bioavailability, limiting the antioxidant benefits it can provide. Elemental Water’s clean formulation ensures the hydrogen retains its potency, providing maximum efficacy in every sip.</p>",
            "bordered": false
          }
        },
        "block_text_d8UjRh": {
          "type": "block_text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "References",
            "text": "<ol><li><strong>Oxidative Stress and Its Role in Parkinson’s Disease</strong><br/>National Center for Biotechnology Information. (2021). <em>Oxidative stress is involved in the pathogenesis of Parkinson’s disease and hydrogen has shown promise in animal models of PD.</em> <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8519836/#:~:text=Oxidative%20stress%20is%20involved%20in,in%20animal%20models%20of%20PD.\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a></li><li><strong>Hydrogen-Rich Water and Health Outcomes</strong><br/>National Center for Biotechnology Information. (2022). <em>Studies have shown that hydrogen-rich water can help reduce oxidative stress and improve certain health outcomes.</em> <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9222692/\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a></li><li><strong>Effects of Hydrogen-Rich Water Supplementation</strong><br/>National Center for Biotechnology Information. (2021). <em>HRW supplementation has been shown to improve physical function in middle-aged men and women.</em> <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8139351/#:~:text=HRW%20supplementation%20has%20been%20shown,men%20and%20women%20%5B18%5D.\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a></li><li><strong>Hydrogen-Rich Water and Reduced Oxidative Stress</strong><br/>National Library of Medicine. (2011). <em>Hydrogen-rich water reduces oxidative stress and improves liver function in chronic hepatitis B patients.</em> <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22146004/\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a></li><li><strong>Antioxidant Effect of Hydrogen in Acute Stroke</strong><br/>National Library of Medicine. (2009). <em>The study shows hydrogen gas can be used as an antioxidant to treat acute stroke.</em> <a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19083400/\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a></li></ol>",
            "bordered": true
          }
